gistration doesn't\n   include calendar scopes. I could not verify this (no external calls made), so\n   it is the most likely cause, not a confirmed one. Fix: default scopes are back\n   to the previously working set; `INTERVALS_SCOPES` env var re-enables the\n   calendar scopes once the client is allowed them at Intervals.icu. Calendar\n   push will need that registration change.\n\n3. **Connection \"expired\" after an hour.** Intervals' token response had no\n   `expires_in` and no `refresh_token` (tokens last until revoked). The code\n   assumed a 3600s default TTL, and with no refresh token the refresher marked the\n   connection expired. Fix: expiry is only scheduled when the provider sends\n   `expires_in`; otherwise the token is non-expiring. The refresher also no longer\n   crashes on a refresh response lacking `expires_in`.\n\nNot tested against the real Intervals.icu (not contacted).\nE\npython3 -c \"import ast;ast.parse(open('server.py').read())\"; git diff --stat"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6165,"cache_read_input_tokens":22320,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6165},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"47733834-16ed-4de2-9076-97250bd824d7","uuid":"dd2cfc7f-362a-4deb-a613-cb37e2440126","timestamp":"2026-10-20T23:32:55.589Z","request_id":"req_011CgEMyAn9fucG3sCYJnBRc","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01YQYhwjBbBzoEnxmjn9ruPA":{"command":"cd /tmp/h-XTwN7W; python3 - <<'E'\ns=open('server.py').read()\ns=s.replace('''    expires_in = int(tok.get(\"expires_in\") or DEFAULT_TOKEN_TTL)\n    refresh = tok.get(\"refresh_token\")\n    if not refresh:\n        log(f\"{user_id}: no refresh_token in response, scheduling expiry in {expir