{"duration_api_ms":29774,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"47733834-16ed-4de2-9076-97250bd824d7","total_cost_usd":0.1073111,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14815,"cache_read_input_tokens":88051,"output_tokens":3923,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1115},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14815,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":643,"cache_read_input_tokens":28485,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3198,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3198},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5-5":{"inputTokens":8,"outputTokens":3923,"cacheReadInputTokens":88051,"cacheCreationInputTokens":14815,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.1073111,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":1115,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":4,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I found three causes and changed the code for each, but I haven't run anything. I only checked that `server.py` parses. I made no calls to Intervals.icu, so the second cause is my best inference, not a confirmed fact. The causes are written up in `ANSWER.md`.\n\n1. **Connect button fails for everyone.**\n   - **Cause:** the button was a plain link, and a browser navigation can't send the `Authorization: Bearer` header. The server saw no user and answered 401.\n   - **Fix:** `auth/init` now returns the authorize URL as JSON. The button fetches it with the header, then sends the browser there. The changes are in `server.py` and `static/app.js`.\n\n2. **Authorize link answers 400 `invalid_request`.**\n   - **Cause (inferred):** the only change before this started was the calendar sync on 2026-10-02, which added `CALENDAR:READ` and `CALENDAR:WRITE` scopes. Rivera's earlier grant had only `ACTIVITY:WRITE` and `WELLNESS:READ`, so the client registration at Intervals.icu probably doesn't allow calendar scopes.\n   - **Fix:** `config.py` now requests the three scopes that worked before. An `INTERVALS_SCOPES` environment variable lets you add the calendar scopes back once the registration allows them.\n   - **Consequence:** pushing workouts to the calendar won't work until that registration change is made.\n\n3. **Rivera told to reconnect after an hour.**\n   - **Cause:** Intervals' token response has no `expires_in` and no `refresh_token`. The code assumed a 3600-second lifetime, and with nothing to refresh with, it marked the connection expired.\n   - **Fix:** expiry is only scheduled when the provider sends `expires_in`. Otherwise the token is treated as non-expiring. The refresher also no longer crashes on a refresh response that lacks `expires_in`.","ttft_ms":2533,"type":"result","duration_ms":30441,"uuid":"1161acb7-26eb-47dc-bc49-90acf84553d2","ttft_stream_ms":1660,"time_to_request_ms":655,"first_content_frame_ms":1660,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
